<http://data.silknow.org/object/b522902b-6afe-31e3-bd25-9d3a84d5c1fe/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "White linen with a design of double headed eagles, etc., woven with pink cotton. To one edge is sewed a piece of marcamé or knotted lace, made of white and pink thread. Borders like this are made by the peasants of Styria to be used upon their sheets and pillow-cases."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/b522902b-6afe-31e3-bd25-9d3a84d5c1fe> .

